## 1. What This System Design Tutorial Is About

This complete system design tutorial covers **scalability, reliability, data handling, and high-level architecture**, with **clear explanations, real-world examples, and practical strategies**.
It teaches the **core concepts you need to know for a system design interview** and is designed as a **complete crash course** for job interviews.

A system design interview does **not focus heavily on coding**. Interviewers do not want to see you write actual code. Instead, they want to understand **how you glue an entire system together**, how different components interact, and how decisions are made at scale.
That is exactly what this tutorial focuses on.

Before designing large-scale distributed systems, it is important to understand the **high-level architecture of an individual computer** and how different components work together to execute code.

